      "pins": ["J1.4", "U2.49", "U2.35", "R7.1", "U4.19", "U4.20"],
      "nets": ["DISP_SDA"],
      "observed": "The net named DISP_SDA contains not only the intended display SDA nodes, but also J1 pin 4 (SWCLK) and U2 pin 49 (PA14).",
      "expected": "DISP_SDA should connect only U2 pin 35 (PB14), R7 pin 1, and U4 pins 19/20 (D1/D2). The Tag-Connect SWCLK line should be on a separate SWCLK net, normally tied to the MCU SWCLK pin (PA14 on this MCU).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"3\") (name \"DISP_SDA\") ... (node (ref \"J1\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"SWCLK\") ...) ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"49\") (pinfunction \"PA14\") ...) ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"35\") (pinfunction \"PB14\") ...) ... (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"D1\") ...) ... (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"20\") (pinfunction \"D2\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "DISP_SDA: U2 pin 35 (`PB14`) — R7 (10 kΩ) to VCC — U4 pins 19/20 (`D1`/`D2`)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "J1 ... pins are VCC, GND, ~{RESET}, SWCLK, SWDIO, SWO"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The SWD programming clock is shorted to the OLED I2C data bus and to MCU PA14. This can prevent reliable SWD programming/debugging, corrupt display communication, and create bus contention between the MCU and the programmer.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show a clear anomaly: the DISP_SDA net is merged with the SWD SWCLK line and MCU PA14, which contradicts the intended separate display I2C and SWD interfaces."
}

